{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonCategory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonCategory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonMTCInput","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_conj_object","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_conj_object","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonCategory.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**The categorical quantum dimension is conjugation-symmetric**: `qDimObj (Xᘁ) = qDimObj X`.\n\nThe corpus fact `qDim_conj`, at last unconditional.  `qDimObj` is by definition the braided\nquantum dimension taken against the canonical right dual, so this is\n`QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_rightDual` read through that definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_unit","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonCategory.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**The categorical quantum dimension of the monoidal unit (the vacuum object) is `1`.**\n`qDimObj (𝟙_C) = 𝟙 (𝟙_C)`.  This is the categorical fact behind the RT-input normalization\n`RibbonMTCInput.vac_dim_one`: when the vacuum label's simple object is the unit, its dimension is\ngenuinely the identity endomorphism of `𝟙_C`, not merely a posited scalar.  It is also the trivial\ncase of conjugation symmetry — `dim(𝟙) = 1 = dim(𝟙ᘁ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_of_unitPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Ribbon.qDim_of_unitPairing","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonCategory.lean#L77-L99","doc":"**The braided quantum dimension of the unit collapses to the identity.**  For the exact pairing\n`𝟙_C ⊣ Y` of the monoidal unit with any right dual `Y`, the braided (twistless) trace\n`η_{𝟙,Y} ≫ β_{𝟙,Y} ≫ ε_{𝟙,Y}` equals `𝟙_{𝟙_C}`.  The braiding of the unit is a pair of unitors\n(`braiding_tensorUnit_left`), and the snake identity (`ExactPairing.evaluation_coevaluation'`),\nwhiskered by `𝟙_C` (conjugation by the right unitor), forces the composite to be the identity.\n(`RightRigidCategory` is omitted — only the unit's exact pairing is needed.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}